# A road runs on past a street's last plot. A new street never runs over
# another road's end without a crossroads: it ends short of it instead.
> new empty
> free on
> construction off
> build crossroads at s0:31
  #1 intersection at s0:31-33, done
> ride #last
  rider: s0:32 facing +
> turn up
  rider: s1:131 facing +
> ride +30
  rider: s1:161 facing +
> build crossroads here
  #61 intersection at s1:160-162, done
> ride #last
  rider: s1:161 facing +
> turn up
  rider: s2:131 facing +
> ride +30
  rider: s2:161 facing +
> build crossroads here
  #103 intersection at s2:160-162, done
# the third street runs south at column 2, past the main street's west end
> streets
  s0  runs east (lots on its north side), cells 10..252
  s1  runs north (lots on its west side), cells 10..252, from crossroads #1
  s2  runs west (lots on its south side), cells 10..252, from crossroads #61
  s3  runs south (lots on its east side), cells 10..252, from crossroads #103
    crossroads #1: s0:32 = s1:131 (cell A32)
    crossroads #61: s1:161 = s2:131 (cell AE32)
    crossroads #103: s2:161 = s3:131 (cell AE2)
